; pasta_t sandbox-setup permissions missing from container-selinux on Fedora 44
; kernel 7.0.11.
;
; pasta(1) sandboxes itself at startup by creating a new user+mount namespace,
; writing uid/gid maps, mounting a tmpfs at /tmp, then pivot_root(2)'ing into
; it. Two groups of permissions are missing from container-selinux's pasta_t:
;
;   cap_userns { setuid setgid } — pasta writes /proc/self/{uid,gid}_map from
;     inside the new user namespace; the kernel checks these capabilities
;     against the namespace the write originates from (cap_userns class), not
;     the outer namespace (capability class).
;
;   tmpfs_t:dir { mounton } — /tmp on this host is a tmpfs, so its label is
;     tmpfs_t. pasta mounts a fresh tmpfs on top of it; that requires mounton
;     permission on the target directory's type.
;
; These should be fixed upstream in container-selinux; track the issue there
; and remove this module once the fix ships in the distro package.
(allow pasta_t self (cap_userns (setgid setuid)))
(allow pasta_t tmpfs_t (dir (mounton)))
